cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DownlinkPick"
abstract: ""Downlink selection when the contact is shorter than the queue — recorded-data inventory with value, age, expiry, dependencies and compressibility against a contact plan, producing a selection plus the marginal value of the next unit of contact time and the identity of what was left behind; greedy value-density baseline scored against an exact multi-knapsack MILP over windows, learned value model and compressibility predictor benchmarked against declared-value passthrough and a size/age heuristic, selection stability under perturbed value estimates measured because a selector that flips on noise is unusable regardless of its optimality.""
type: software
